      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The region that became Clayton was part of Concordia Parish, one of Louisiana's original parishes formed in 1807 from territory acquired in the 1803 Louisiana Purchase.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/clayton_louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cotton remains a principal commodity in Clayton, reflecting the area's long agricultural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clayton%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Clayton sits on the Tensas River, a popular spot for fishing and boating, and the Army Corps of Engineers maintains a boat launch there.",
